Task: Implement ParentLock component

Summary:
Created src/components/ParentLock.ts implementing the hold-for-3-seconds
parental lock mechanism using Phaser input events. The component registers
pointerdown/pointerup/pointerout listeners on a target game object, starts
a timer on pointerdown, fires onSuccess when the timer completes (default
3000ms), and fires onFailure (canceling the timer) when the pointer is
released or leaves the target before the hold duration elapses.

Key Design Decisions:
- Used arrow function class properties for handlePointerDown/handlePointerUp
  to preserve 'this' binding when used as Phaser event callbacks. This avoids
  passing a context parameter to on()/off(), which is important for testability
  since the mock event emitter calls callbacks without 'this' binding.
- Used import type Phaser from 'phaser' for type-only imports (verbatimModuleSyntax).
- ParentLockOptions interface accepts Phaser.Scene and Phaser.GameObjects.GameObject.
- Timer is stored as Phaser.Time.TimerEvent | null, cancelled via remove().

Files Created:
- src/components/ParentLock.ts (91 lines)

Class API:
- constructor(options: ParentLockOptions): Registers 3 event listeners
- destroy(): Removes all listeners and cancels active timer
- handlePointerDown (private): Starts delayedCall timer
- handlePointerUp (private): Cancels timer, fires onFailure if active

